loom scan=caravan_ladder_carry modules=107 bodies=18039 distinct=7841 copies=10198 carried_lines=137176 ceiling=137300
loom scan=caravan_edge_order api=object-api.xml method=Retype errors=7 verdict=alphabetical

file caravan/edge.rye the edge -- three refusals asked of the request alone, in an order Caravan chose and states
file tools/caravan_edge_witness.rish the witness -- three RED paths, three published sentences bound two-sidedly, the fan-out limit read both ways it is stated
file tools/fixtures/caravan_edge_control.sh the three plants -- a reversed order, two checks collapsed into one answer, an alignment check welcoming every address
file tools/fixtures/caravan_edge_order_scan.sh the standing question -- does seL4 publish a check order, or only a reading order
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish the rung registered -- bijection whole at 104
file tools/caravan_ladder_spine_witness.rish module pin 106 -> 107
file tools/caravan_ladder_print_witness.rish module pin 106 -> 107, holding read from the scan at 43 rather than incremented
file tools/caravan_ladder_carry_witness.rish module pin 106 -> 107 and the carry re-measured at 137,176
file caravan/README.md the edge section -- the one moment, the unpublished order, the two lines kept apart, and the agenda deliberately left open
file crux/REMEMBER.md live edge and Now refilled; the next rung named as the policy table rather than as a finish

recommend keep-going Teaching `capabilities.rye`'s policy table to answer through its neighbours is the next rung and it is ungated: every owed refusal now has a module answering it, yet `refusals.rye` rightly still counts seven, because its count is what the table can reach and the table has not learned to speak through the tree, the buffer, the region, or the edge. Closing the agenda by measurement rather than by proximity is the crux, and it is exactly the shape `refusals.rye` named for itself. The one gate worth Keaton's eye stays small and unchanged: jinja2 and ply on the pier's Python environment open five more libsel4 headers in a single step.
